Qudit states
d = 1 state corresponds to a one-dimensional Hilbert space and is therefore a trivial quantum system.[17]
Qubit – Qudit with d = 2 states
Qutrit – Qudit with d = 3 states
Ququart or Ququat – Qudit with d = 4 states
Ququint– Qudit with d = 5 states
Quhexit – Qudit with d = 6 states [18]
Quoctit – Qudit with d = 8 states
Quit – Audit with prime number dimensions (commonly used in quantum error correction)

